    },
    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "Hi @echasnovski \r\nThanks for making this awesome plugin.\r\n\r\nRelated to mini.jump2d, I would like to ask a concern that does it support jump within a region selection, like https://github.com/mfussenegger/nvim-treehopper does?\r\n\r\nThank you!",
    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Hi <a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/echasnovski/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski\">@echasnovski</a><br>\nThanks for making this awesome plugin.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related to mini.jump2d, I would like to ask a concern that does it support jump within a region selection, like <a href=\"https://github.com/mfussenegger/nvim-treehopper\">https://github.com/mfussenegger/nvim-treehopper</a> does?</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Thank you!</p>",
    "bodyText": "Hi @echasnovski\nThanks for making this awesome plugin.\nRelated to mini.jump2d, I would like to ask a concern that does it support jump within a region selection, like https://github.com/mfussenegger/nvim-treehopper does?\nThank you!",
    "category": {
        "createdAt": "2022-01-02T14:24:09Z",
        "description": "Ask the community for help",
        "emoji": ":pray:",
        "emojiHTML": "<div>🙏</div>",
        "id": "DIC_kwDOFoksYM4CAgqN",
        "isAnswerable": true,
        "name": "Q&A",
        "slug": "q-a",
        "updatedAt": "2022-01-02T14:24:09Z"
    },
    "closed": false,
    "closedAt": null,
    "comment_count": 1,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author": {
                "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24854248?u=d09fd974c6720eba3039db6beb2f1c1efecdb51d&v=4",
                "login": "echasnovski",
                "resourcePath": "/echasnovski",
                "url": "https://github.com/echasnovski"
            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> Hi @echasnovski Thanks for making this awesome plugin.\r\n> \r\n> Related to mini.jump2d, I would like to ask a concern that does it support jump within a region selection, like https://github.com/mfussenegger/nvim-treehopper does?\r\n> \r\n> Thank you!\r\n\r\nHi!\r\n\r\nI am not entirely sure what this plugin does about region selection. If it selects region based on tree-sitter nodes, then no: 'mini.jump2d' is meant as jumping to spots. For selecting custom regions there are [mini.ai](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/readmes/mini-ai.md) and incremental selection in 'nvim-treesitter' itself.\r\n\r\nJumping based on tree-sitter nodes, however, is an interesting idea and seems to be totally doable with a custom spotter. It is not a builtin, though. If this functionality is critical to you and you don't have time to implement custom spotter yourself, open an issue and I'll take a look at it when I get time.",
            "bodyHTML": "<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Hi <a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/echasnovski/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski\">@echasnovski</a> Thanks for making this awesome plugin.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related to mini.jump2d, I would like to ask a concern that does it support jump within a region selection, like <a href=\"https://github.com/mfussenegger/nvim-treehopper\">https://github.com/mfussenegger/nvim-treehopper</a> does?</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Thank you!</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Hi!</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I am not entirely sure what this plugin does about region selection. If it selects region based on tree-sitter nodes, then no: 'mini.jump2d' is meant as jumping to spots. For selecting custom regions there are <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/readmes/mini-ai.md\">mini.ai</a> and incremental selection in 'nvim-treesitter' itself.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Jumping based on tree-sitter nodes, however, is an interesting idea and seems to be totally doable with a custom spotter. It is not a builtin, though. If this functionality is critical to you and you don't have time to implement custom spotter yourself, open an issue and I'll take a look at it when I get time.</p>",
            "bodyText": "Hi @echasnovski Thanks for making this awesome plugin.\nRelated to mini.jump2d, I would like to ask a concern that does it support jump within a region selection, like https://github.com/mfussenegger/nvim-treehopper does?\nThank you!\n\nHi!\nI am not entirely sure what this plugin does about region selection. If it selects region based on tree-sitter nodes, then no: 'mini.jump2d' is meant as jumping to spots. For selecting custom regions there are mini.ai and incremental selection in 'nvim-treesitter' itself.\nJumping based on tree-sitter nodes, however, is an interesting idea and seems to be totally doable with a custom spotter. It is not a builtin, though. If this functionality is critical to you and you don't have time to implement custom spotter yourself, open an issue and I'll take a look at it when I get time.",
